  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ELIMINATE: Elodea Management Initiative for St. Naum Springs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ELIMINATE is a 12-month initiative addressing the invasive Elodea canadensis threatening St. Naum Springs in North Macedonia. Focused on community collaboration, the project aims to reduce Elodea coverage by 80%, restoring native habitats and water quality. Empowering 50 trained community members ensures ongoing management, fostering resilience, and sustaining eco-tourism. With a $26,000 budget, ELIMINATE combines workshops, removal campaigns, and awareness to protect this UNESCO-listed site, promoting a participatory and sustainable approach for a thriving ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
